pcm: fold the voice loop's address-step boolean algebra

Each of the four address steps in the voice loop, and the matching one in the
pseudo-slot 31 generator, computes

    add = (!cmp && b6 && !b15) || (!cmp && !b6);
    sub =  !cmp && b6 &&  b15;
    cnt = b7 ? cnt - (add - sub) : cnt + (add - sub);

(add - sub) has only three values: 0 when cmp, -1 when (b6 && b15), +1
otherwise. b7 is fixed for the slot, so the whole thing is one signed step whose
direction is a loop-invariant. The `kon ||` in the select above it cannot change
the outcome either: when (!b6 && address_cmp) holds the selected value is
address_loop whichever arm is taken, and when it does not, both arms are
address_cnt. Both rewrites are exact, not approximations.

pcm.config.reg_slots is also read three times per slot iteration -- the loop
bound, the slot2 select and the last-slot test. Nothing inside PCM_Update can
write it (PCM_Write is the only writer and is never called from here), but the
compiler reloads it anyway because the slot pointers alias into the same object.
Hoisted into a local.

Measured on the ROM-free voice-loop harness, all 32 voices keyed on:
32458 -> 31543 Ir per tick (-2.8%).

